From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Stop incomplete CSI/OSC sequence length at the NUL terminator

An unfinished sequence reaches str[i] == NUL. Returning i+1 then advances
callers past the string terminator. Complete sequences still include their
final byte; truncated sequences now stop immediately before the terminator.
Original downstream static review of official 4.0.0. No upstream writes.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
--- a/pick.c
+++ b/pick.c
@@ -629 +629 @@ skipescseq(const char *str)
-	return i + 1;
+	return i + (str[i] != '\0');
